The '''ALGS: 2026 Split 1 Playoffs''' is the first event in the 26-27 ALGS Calendar. Initially announced after the [[Apex_Legends_Global_Series/2026/Championship|ALGS 2026 Championship]]. The event is held in Paris, France. Although originally announced to be in Riyadh, the EWC announced their relocation to Paris on May 20th.<ref name="EWC PRS">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/2057121960623006162|title=Esports World Cup 2026 is coming to Paris|author=[[Esports World Cup]]}}</ref> The Split 1 playoffs also ties in to be a part of the [[esports:Esports World Cup/2026|2026 Esports World Cup]] 

:''See [[esports:Esports World Cup/2026|here]] to read about the Esports World Cup 2026, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''

==Format==
===Group Stage===
* 40 teams will be split into 4 even groups of 10 teams each and compete in the {{Abbr/RoundRobin}}
* Each team will play in 3 {{Abbr/MatchSeries/6}} (a total of 18 games) in the ''Group Stage''.
** {{bgcolortext|up|Top 14 teams}} of the stage will advance to the '''Finals'''.
** {{bgcolortext|stay|15th - 34th teams}} of the stage will advance to the '''Survivor Stage'''.
** {{bgcolortext|down|Bottom 6 teams}} are '''Eliminated'''.

===Survivor Stage===
* 20 teams will in a series of 10 games.
** {{bgcolortext|up|Top 6 teams}} advance to the '''Finals'''.
** {{bgcolortext|down|7-20th placed teams}} are '''Eliminated'''.

===Finals===
* The 20 remaining teams will compete in the {{Abbr/MatchPoint/50}}


