==About==
The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established '''Gamers8''' series. '''Apex Legends''' was announced as part of the line-up on April 12, 2024.<ref name="EWC APEX">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ESWCgg/status/1778709651955302809|title=#ApexLegends enters the arena!|date=2024-04-12|author=Esports World Cup|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>
:''See [https://liquipedia.net/esports/Esports_World_Cup/2024 here] to read about the Esports World Cup 2024, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''

==Format==
===Bracket Stage===
* '''Group Stage:''' 
** 40 teams will be split into 2 even groups of 20 teams each and compete in a series of 10 games.
*** {{bgcolortext|up|Top 9 teams}} of each group will advance to the ''Finals''.
*** {{bgcolortext|stay|10-19 placed teams}} of each group will advance to the ''Last Chance''.
*** {{bgcolortext|down|20th placed teams}} are eliminated.
* '''Last Chance:''' 
** 20 teams will in a series of 10 games.
*** {{bgcolortext|up|Top 2 teams}} advance to the ''Finals''.
*** {{bgcolortext|down|3-20th placed teams}} are eliminated.

===Finals===
* '''Finals:''' ''August 4th''
** The 20 remaining teams will compete in the {{Abbr/MatchPoint/60}}
** The 18 teams that advanced from the ''Group Stage'' will start the ''Finals'' with '''Advance Starting Points''' based off their placements of ''Winners Bracket''.

